SSVEP EEG Dataset
=================

Description
-----------
This dataset contains EEG recordings during a Steady-State Visual Evoked Potential (SSVEP)
flicker paradigm. Participants viewed flickering visual stimuli at specific frequencies
(13 Hz and 17 Hz) to elicit frequency-tagged neural responses in occipital cortex.

Equipment
---------
- EEG System: Nexstem (Board ID: Nex-Dev-00370, v27)
- DAQ: NI-DAQ USB-6008
- Sampling Rate: 2000 Hz
- Electrode Type: Dry electrodes
- EEG Channels: O1, O2 (occipital)
- Reference: Cz
- Ground: T7
- DRL: T8

Data Processing
---------------
Raw CSV files are provided without preprocessing.

Paradigm
--------
- Flicker frequencies: 13 Hz and 17 Hz
- Test condition: Visual flicker stimulation for 20 seconds
- Rest condition: No stimulation for 10 seconds
- Number of trials: 6 (alternating frequencies)
- Total paradigm duration: ~180 seconds

Recording Location
------------------
Anthriq Lab

Contact
-------
Anthriq 
